1
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,767
Do you want to make it real,
like we're in a relationship?

2
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:25,907
<i>Oh my, does Nero have telepathic skills
that he can read my mind?</i>

3
00:00:27,576 --> 00:00:29,644
<i>Does he want to kiss me?</i>

4
00:00:30,579 --> 00:00:33,548
You're holding my hand so tightly.

5
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:35,651
You can let go now.

6
00:00:35,651 --> 00:00:37,952
No one is...

7
00:00:38,601 --> 00:00:40,269
looking.

8
00:00:43,183 --> 00:00:45,519
I'm sure you're not stupid.

9
00:00:45,527 --> 00:00:46,666
Do you really think

10
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:48,601
that Nero will just have
a new girlfriend overnight?

11
00:00:48,601 --> 00:00:53,168
I'm not one to make silly assumptions
when it comes to other people.

12
00:00:53,168 --> 00:00:56,338
The fact is, Nero and I are over.

13
00:00:56,338 --> 00:00:59,334
So, he can do whatever he wants.

14
00:00:59,334 --> 00:01:02,337
If there's something that bothers me,
that's you.

15
00:01:02,337 --> 00:01:03,334
I thought you'd be interested

16
00:01:03,334 --> 00:01:06,508
to know the real score
between Nero and Florence.

17
00:01:06,508 --> 00:01:11,628
And I thought you're interested to know

18
00:01:11,628 --> 00:01:13,365
that all of this is just an act.

19
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:15,484
Who is she in your lives?

20
00:01:15,484 --> 00:01:16,785
She's our cook.

21
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:20,289
Are you telling me all this

22
00:01:20,289 --> 00:01:23,358
because you want me to break them apart?

23
00:01:23,358 --> 00:01:25,961
This is a dangerous playground
that you're in.

24
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:27,429
And it looks like you and Nero

25
00:01:27,429 --> 00:01:31,296
are about to be involved
in a seriously complicated situation.

26
00:01:31,296 --> 00:01:34,937
Are there any problems with my ideas?

27
00:01:34,937 --> 00:01:37,506
Are there things you don't like,
or do you want to add something?

28
00:01:37,506 --> 00:01:41,089
It seems that's not what we're expecting

29
00:01:41,089 --> 00:01:43,946
to talk about in this meeting.

30
00:01:43,946 --> 00:01:45,580
Huh? Why?

31
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,582
What should we talk about?

32
00:01:47,582 --> 00:01:49,084
About the Grand GU Ball.

33
00:01:49,084 --> 00:01:50,152
Yes.

34
00:01:50,152 --> 00:01:52,120
Grand GU Ball?

35
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,189
Weren't you informed, Florence?

36
00:01:54,189 --> 00:01:57,092
It's the most important event here in GU.

37
00:01:57,092 --> 00:01:59,594
So as our student representative,

38
00:01:59,594 --> 00:02:02,631
I think it's a good idea
that we should all brainstorm

39
00:02:02,631 --> 00:02:04,299
for this upcoming event.

40
00:02:04,299 --> 00:02:06,034
I'm sorry, Florence,

41
00:02:06,034 --> 00:02:09,004
but the Grand GU Ball is not just a party.

42
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,673
Yes, and this year is very important.

43
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:15,444
That's because the Com Arts are
the designated host of this grand event.

44
00:02:15,444 --> 00:02:18,591
Maybe I'm also pressured
with being the student representative.

45
00:02:18,591 --> 00:02:19,981
Think about it,

46
00:02:19,981 --> 00:02:26,822
I thought of a lot of ideas and projects
to make our university better

47
00:02:26,822 --> 00:02:30,492
but then, all they want to talk about
is just one thing,

48
00:02:30,492 --> 00:02:33,195
the Grand GU Ball.

49
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:34,828
What hurts the most,

50
00:02:34,828 --> 00:02:37,632
is I don't understand anything
about what they're talking about.

51
00:02:37,632 --> 00:02:39,968
If there's something
you don't understand in this world,

52
00:02:39,968 --> 00:02:42,237
don't hesitate to ask me.

53
00:02:42,237 --> 00:02:43,605
That's the least I can do.

54
00:02:43,605 --> 00:02:44,673
Thank you.

55
00:02:44,673 --> 00:02:46,375
It's still early.

56
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:48,276
Let's eat first.

57
00:02:48,276 --> 00:02:52,914
Soup? 450 pesos per bowl?

58
00:02:52,914 --> 00:02:54,456
What's that?

59
00:02:54,456 --> 00:02:56,885
Do the ingredients have gold dust?
Why is it so expensive?

60
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:58,385
I'm hungry okay?

61
00:02:58,385 --> 00:02:59,688
Stop overreacting.

62
00:02:59,688 --> 00:03:01,197
I'll be the one who will pay for it.

63
00:03:01,197 --> 00:03:03,330
Overreacting, Nero? Me?

64
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:04,726
They're overpriced.

65
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:07,195
No! This is a luxury, Nero.

66
00:03:07,195 --> 00:03:09,778
And besides, there are a lot of
cheap eateries in the area

67
00:03:09,778 --> 00:03:11,666
that are delicious.

68
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:13,335
So, if you want to eat, go ahead.

69
00:03:13,335 --> 00:03:15,137
I will not eat here.

70
00:03:15,137 --> 00:03:18,073
Whatever is left, I'll donate to charity.

71
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:20,008
Okay fine,

72
00:03:20,008 --> 00:03:23,429
where is this place
accepted by your moral standards?

73
00:04:21,903 --> 00:04:23,906
Are you smiling?

74
00:04:25,273 --> 00:04:31,513
Mister, one more isaw, betamax,
and chicken ass.

75
00:04:31,513 --> 00:04:32,814
Hey, what's with you?

76
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,449
You became serious all of a sudden
when I saw you smiling.

77
00:04:34,449 --> 00:04:37,252
Too bad, whatever you do,
I already saw you smiling.

78
00:04:37,252 --> 00:04:40,055
I can't unsee that anymore.
Come on, smile one more time.

79
00:04:40,055 --> 00:04:42,257
Smile... Smile.

80
00:04:42,257 --> 00:04:44,860
You're so grouchy.

81
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:47,762
You know, that smile of yours,

82
00:04:47,762 --> 00:04:51,166
Antonia must see that whenever she sees you.

83
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:53,502
Because I'm sure
that if she sees you smiling,

84
00:04:53,502 --> 00:04:54,903
she'll reconcile with you,

85
00:04:54,903 --> 00:04:59,030
because her heart will melt
if she sees you smiling.

86
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,848
Smile... Come on, smile.

87
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:08,984
Just one more smile. Smile.

88
00:05:08,984 --> 00:05:11,820
Come on, smile now.

89
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:12,921
Just one.

90
00:05:12,921 --> 00:05:15,290
Hurry. Don't be too stingy with your smiles.

91
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:16,991
Just one smile.

92
00:05:27,802 --> 00:05:30,906
You're holding back your smile.

93
00:05:30,906 --> 00:05:32,307
You're holding back your smile.

94
00:05:32,307 --> 00:05:34,470
You know what?

95
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:37,783
Now that I made you smile,
let's go back to talking about cheap food.

96
00:05:37,783 --> 00:05:39,414
Did you think
I've already forgotten about it?

97
00:05:39,414 --> 00:05:42,417
You know, I can't really accept
where you took me earlier.

98
00:05:42,417 --> 00:05:43,451
Imagine, just soup...

99
00:05:43,451 --> 00:05:45,487
that kind of soup, the serving is so small.

100
00:05:45,487 --> 00:05:47,322
I think one cup of rice
is much bigger than that.

101
00:05:47,322 --> 00:05:49,991
How much was that? 350 or 450 pesos?
It was so expensive.

102
00:05:49,991 --> 00:05:52,594
Here, the cheapest price is 7 pesos,

103
00:05:52,594 --> 00:05:54,462
while in that restaurant,

104
00:05:54,462 --> 00:05:57,399
I think the lowest price
is the appetizer at 350 pesos.

105
00:05:57,399 --> 00:06:00,702
Here, look at this at 20 pesos,
you'll have all the meat.

106
00:06:00,702 --> 00:06:02,282
It's worth it already.

107
00:06:02,282 --> 00:06:03,675
You, rich people,

108
00:06:03,675 --> 00:06:06,942
are so used to
that kind of luxury restaurant.

109
00:06:06,942 --> 00:06:10,812
If you'll buy here
and use up all your money here...

110
00:06:10,812 --> 00:06:13,014
Come hurry, smile.

111
00:06:20,121 --> 00:06:22,257
<i>She makes you hopeful.</i>

112
00:06:22,257 --> 00:06:24,701
<i>She makes you brave.</i>

113
00:06:24,701 --> 00:06:29,201
Brave enough that you can be happy.

114
00:06:29,201 --> 00:06:31,942
And she makes you understand
that in order to be happy,

115
00:06:31,942 --> 00:06:37,372
you have to embrace it,
grab it, and choose it.

116
00:06:37,372 --> 00:06:41,809
And when the opportunity comes,
you shouldn't be scared.

117
00:07:10,839 --> 00:07:12,741
Smile.

118
00:07:12,741 --> 00:07:14,776
Come on, smile now. Just one.

119
00:07:14,776 --> 00:07:18,045
Hurry. Don't be too stingy with your smiles.

120
00:07:20,018 --> 00:07:22,220
Are you smiling?

121
00:07:23,285 --> 00:07:29,257
Mister, one more isaw,
betamax, and chicken ass.

122
00:07:32,227 --> 00:07:35,563
He's more cowboy than me.

123
00:07:37,766 --> 00:07:43,004
So, his favorite fruit is rambutan.

124
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:49,510
And it seems that his favorite food
is grilled stuff at Hepa Lane.

125
00:07:50,211 --> 00:07:52,380
Good job, Florencia.

126
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:56,984
You're slowly solving Nero's mysterious side.

127
00:07:58,987 --> 00:08:01,022
In fairness...

128
00:08:01,823 --> 00:08:04,859
he's fun to be with.

129
00:08:06,428 --> 00:08:09,530
His future girlfriend will be lucky.

130
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:38,993
I am my own woman,

131
00:08:38,993 --> 00:08:42,530
I can handle everything
that will be thrown at me.

132
00:08:43,465 --> 00:08:45,733
But, you're right.

133
00:08:53,141 --> 00:08:54,776
You're something else.

134
00:08:54,776 --> 00:08:57,745
You have a strong influence on me.

135
00:09:01,649 --> 00:09:04,819
- Who?
- Oh my God!

136
00:09:04,819 --> 00:09:06,621
Stop sneaking in!

137
00:09:06,621 --> 00:09:10,057
You always enter a frame without a set-up.

138
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:13,027
What's that?

139
00:09:13,027 --> 00:09:15,096
Do you want to find out?

140
00:09:20,034 --> 00:09:21,369
What's with this place?

141
00:09:21,369 --> 00:09:23,972
Just wait.

142
00:09:23,972 --> 00:09:26,107
You even have lights.

143
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:27,896
Come here.

144
00:09:32,747 --> 00:09:36,684
Hold that... and spread it out there.

145
00:09:39,988 --> 00:09:41,589
Here.

146
00:09:44,058 --> 00:09:45,560
Why do you have a comforter?

147
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:47,562
Well, just play along. Spread it out.

148
00:09:47,562 --> 00:09:49,463
That's it.

149
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:56,037
Lie down.

150
00:09:56,037 --> 00:09:57,579
Lie down.

151
00:10:08,383 --> 00:10:10,001
Lie down.

152
00:10:16,057 --> 00:10:17,959
Lie down.

153
00:10:17,959 --> 00:10:19,227
Wait a second.

154
00:10:19,227 --> 00:10:20,961
Let me just fix this.

155
00:10:21,629 --> 00:10:23,134
There.

156
00:10:24,204 --> 00:10:25,767
Are you ready?

157
00:10:25,767 --> 00:10:28,069
- What?
- Are you ready?

158
00:10:28,069 --> 00:10:30,405
- What?
- I'll count to three...

159
00:10:30,405 --> 00:10:34,209
One, two, three.

160
00:10:34,209 --> 00:10:35,743
- Hey, you pervert!
- Ouch, what's that?

161
00:10:35,743 --> 00:10:36,882
- You pervert!
- Ouch!

162
00:10:36,882 --> 00:10:38,313
You're planning something else, aren't you?

163
00:10:38,313 --> 00:10:39,781
- What do you mean I'm planning?
- You have an evil plan, right?

164
00:10:39,781 --> 00:10:41,783
- What do you mean I'm planning?
- No!

165
00:10:41,783 --> 00:10:43,885
- Let me go!
- Florence, wait! Calm down, okay?

166
00:10:43,885 --> 00:10:46,057
- Just calm down.
- What? What are you doing?

167
00:10:46,057 --> 00:10:48,627
- Here.
- What are you getting from your bag?

168
00:10:48,627 --> 00:10:50,762
- You're going to kill me, right?
- I'm not planning anything.

169
00:10:50,762 --> 00:10:53,232
Wait! I don't have any evil plans.
Here it is.

170
00:10:53,232 --> 00:10:54,695
Here.

171
00:10:56,685 --> 00:10:58,086
What's that?

172
00:10:58,933 --> 00:11:00,701
Here, try it.

173
00:11:03,271 --> 00:11:05,239
Can you be killed by this?

174
00:11:18,935 --> 00:11:20,870
Look up there.

175
00:11:29,964 --> 00:11:31,199
What's this?

176
00:11:31,199 --> 00:11:33,902
What can I see here?

177
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:36,671
- Saturn? Jupiter? Mars?
- There is it.

178
00:11:36,671 --> 00:11:39,868
There... Let me.

179
00:11:41,843 --> 00:11:44,450
Orionids meteor shower.

180
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:47,025
Those are remnants of Halley's Comet.

181
00:11:47,025 --> 00:11:52,615
Imagine, the last time we saw Halley's Comet
was in 1986.

182
00:11:52,615 --> 00:11:58,293
But even now, we can still feel it.

183
00:11:58,293 --> 00:12:01,796
I hope I have that kind of impact
on the person I love.

184
00:12:01,796 --> 00:12:04,766
Even if I'm no longer around,

185
00:12:04,766 --> 00:12:09,402
she can still remember the beautiful memories
that I left for her.

186
00:12:17,245 --> 00:12:19,480
There, look at it.

187
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:22,984
It's over there.

188
00:12:22,984 --> 00:12:24,485
Hurry.

189
00:12:27,555 --> 00:12:29,424
Is it beautiful?

190
00:12:29,424 --> 00:12:31,859
It's beautiful.

191
00:12:31,859 --> 00:12:33,718
It's beautiful.

192
00:12:40,877 --> 00:12:43,984
Yes, it's beautiful.

193
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:51,145
Go ahead and look if it's beautiful.

194
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,914
Okay.

195
00:13:05,793 --> 00:13:08,062
It's really beautiful.

196
00:13:09,998 --> 00:13:11,761
Yes...

197
00:13:12,612 --> 00:13:14,964
it's very beautiful.

198
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:21,809
Let's share.

199
00:13:23,144 --> 00:13:25,813
Okay, you can use the other side.

200
00:13:27,949 --> 00:13:30,651
Your forehead is too big.

201
00:13:32,153 --> 00:13:35,456
- Wait, let's adjust it.
- Did I offend you or not?

202
00:13:35,456 --> 00:13:37,659
Not really. But just for tonight...

203
00:13:37,659 --> 00:13:39,260
- Tomorrow is...
- Well, it's beautiful.

204
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:41,328
Come on, let's look again.

205
00:13:50,438 --> 00:13:54,203
Coffee. So you won't be sleepy
in your class later.

206
00:13:55,406 --> 00:13:56,407
Thank you, Owen.

207
00:13:56,407 --> 00:14:00,281
You're really an angel
just when I need extra strength for today.

208
00:14:00,281 --> 00:14:02,816
Why did you stay up late last night?

209
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:08,222
How did you know I stayed up late last night?

210
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:11,959
It's just a guess because
I saw you yawning now.

211
00:14:13,461 --> 00:14:15,630
Come, why don't you ride with me to school?

212
00:14:15,630 --> 00:14:17,743
Let's go, Florence.

213
00:14:19,767 --> 00:14:22,737
Bro, I'll take Florence to school.

214
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:24,439
I will.

215
00:14:24,439 --> 00:14:26,774
I'm the boyfriend.

216
00:14:26,774 --> 00:14:29,477
Do you mean fake boyfriend?

217
00:14:29,477 --> 00:14:32,714
Besides, I asked her first.

218
00:14:32,714 --> 00:14:35,032
So what?

219
00:14:35,032 --> 00:14:37,452
Basic rule of firsts, Nero.

220
00:14:37,452 --> 00:14:39,557
I don't care.

221
00:14:39,557 --> 00:14:43,194
Remember I told you,
the first chance you get, break it off.

222
00:14:43,194 --> 00:14:45,349
I understand you're trying
to protect Florence,

223
00:14:45,349 --> 00:14:47,330
but this is getting ridiculous.

224
00:14:47,330 --> 00:14:49,232
Florence and I have an agreement.

225
00:14:49,232 --> 00:14:53,036
And she agreed to help me,
so don't meddle anymore.

226
00:14:53,036 --> 00:14:55,839
She agreed or she was forced
because she owes you something?

227
00:14:55,839 --> 00:14:57,307
It doesn't matter.

228
00:14:57,307 --> 00:15:00,042
I will bring her to school.

229
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:03,046
- Let's go, Florence.
- No, she's going with me.

230
00:15:03,046 --> 00:15:04,347
Stop it.

231
00:15:04,347 --> 00:15:05,949
I don't need both of you.

232
00:15:05,949 --> 00:15:08,084
I can go to school on my own.

233
00:15:08,084 --> 00:15:12,900
Here, have some coffee...
so you will both be nervous.

234
00:15:21,329 --> 00:15:23,399
Nero is so possessive, as if we're a couple.

235
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:26,102
- And Owen meanwhile is acting this way.
- What happened?

236
00:15:26,102 --> 00:15:27,437
You were suspended

237
00:15:27,437 --> 00:15:30,740
because of your stupid shenanigan
during the Agora day.

238
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:32,976
You had the guts to do something foolish,

239
00:15:32,976 --> 00:15:35,178
but you didn't do it correctly.

240
00:15:35,178 --> 00:15:36,813
Dad, let me explain.

241
00:15:36,813 --> 00:15:38,781
Dad!

242
00:15:38,781 --> 00:15:40,850
- Hey, excuse me.
- Dad...

243
00:15:40,850 --> 00:15:43,119
You shouldn't hurt her.

244
00:15:43,119 --> 00:15:45,388
Florence, stay out of this.

245
00:15:45,388 --> 00:15:48,791
No, Camille. You shouldn't let someone
hurt you like that.

246
00:15:48,791 --> 00:15:50,059
He's my father.

247
00:15:50,059 --> 00:15:51,294
Still, Camille.

248
00:15:51,294 --> 00:15:55,631
Even if he's your dad, he doesn't have
the right to hurt you that way.

249
00:15:57,467 --> 00:16:01,571
And you... You're a father
but you act that way.

250
00:16:01,571 --> 00:16:03,973
You even look educated.

251
00:16:03,973 --> 00:16:06,542
Are you familiar with RA 9262

252
00:16:06,542 --> 00:16:09,345
Anti Violence against Women and Children?

253
00:16:09,345 --> 00:16:11,247
Hey you, don't meddle!

254
00:16:11,247 --> 00:16:12,715
This is a family matter.

255
00:16:12,715 --> 00:16:16,486
So, just because you're a family,
you can hurt her just like that?

256
00:16:16,486 --> 00:16:19,389
Shouldn't you not hurt her instead?

257
00:16:19,389 --> 00:16:21,357
Because as far as I know, if you're a father,

258
00:16:21,357 --> 00:16:23,446
you should protect your child.

259
00:16:23,446 --> 00:16:26,115
Don't you dare lecture me like I'm a child!

260
00:16:29,198 --> 00:16:31,334
I'm sorry.
You went into beast mode immediately

261
00:16:31,334 --> 00:16:34,770
when you can talk to Camille peacefully.

262
00:16:42,312 --> 00:16:44,480
You're a grandson
of Don Garpidio Ferell, right?

263
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,115
So, don't meddle here or else...

264
00:16:46,115 --> 00:16:48,186
Or else what?

265
00:16:48,186 --> 00:16:49,852
I have no issues with the Ferells.

266
00:16:49,852 --> 00:16:54,324
It's this woman who owes me, so don't meddle.

267
00:16:54,324 --> 00:16:55,391
For your information,

268
00:16:55,391 --> 00:16:58,227
the girl you're messing with
is also a Ferell.

269
00:16:58,227 --> 00:17:01,208
I suggest you back off, Mr. Villarico.

270
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:02,598
Sir, please.

271
00:17:02,598 --> 00:17:05,702
Let's not make decisions
that we'll regret later on.

272
00:17:05,702 --> 00:17:08,128
You speak so arrogantly.

273
00:17:13,242 --> 00:17:15,812
Grandfather Garp...

274
00:17:15,812 --> 00:17:18,490
Yes, Grandfather.

275
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:22,727
Yes, we're with Mr. Villarico,
Camille's father.

276
00:17:25,247 --> 00:17:27,148
Trouble?

277
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:29,759
Guys, are we in trouble?

278
00:17:29,759 --> 00:17:32,033
Grandfather Garp is asking.

279
00:17:32,996 --> 00:17:37,100
Are we, Mr. Villarico?

280
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,626
Let's go.

281
00:17:43,351 --> 00:17:44,741
I will be okay, Florence.

282
00:17:44,741 --> 00:17:46,274
Are you sure?

283
00:17:46,274 --> 00:17:48,009
Yeah.

284
00:17:48,009 --> 00:17:49,544
I'll call you.

285
00:17:49,544 --> 00:17:52,346
- Thank you.
- I'll make sure you're okay.

286
00:18:00,789 --> 00:18:02,424
Huh?

287
00:18:02,424 --> 00:18:03,958
What?

288
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:12,567
Who is that woman you're talking to?

289
00:18:13,401 --> 00:18:15,837
Woman? What do you mean woman?

290
00:18:15,837 --> 00:18:18,740
You're the only woman in my life.

291
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,575
That's Troy.

292
00:18:20,575 --> 00:18:21,776
You're something else.

293
00:18:21,776 --> 00:18:24,179
You easily get jealous.

294
00:18:24,179 --> 00:18:26,247
Me? Jealous?

295
00:18:26,247 --> 00:18:27,649
Please!

296
00:18:27,649 --> 00:18:29,384
What does Troy need?

297
00:18:29,384 --> 00:18:31,086
You know, it was so weird.

298
00:18:31,086 --> 00:18:34,456
All I understood is
there was a Mr. Villarico.

299
00:18:34,456 --> 00:18:37,025
And he even called me Grandfather Garp.

300
00:18:37,025 --> 00:18:38,994
Maybe he's playing a prank.

301
00:18:38,994 --> 00:18:42,263
Serafica, do you want to take a bath?

302
00:18:42,263 --> 00:18:43,765
Excuse me?

303
00:18:43,765 --> 00:18:46,801
Why would I want to bathe with you?

304
00:18:46,801 --> 00:18:48,670
Please!

305
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:53,008
It's more fun to take a bath together.

306
00:18:53,008 --> 00:18:54,209
Serafica...

307
00:18:54,209 --> 00:18:55,910
- What?
- Here I come...

308
00:18:55,910 --> 00:18:58,179
I'm coming I'm here now.

309
00:18:58,179 --> 00:19:00,382
- Stop it. Someone might see us.
- Run now! Go ahead and run.

310
00:19:00,382 --> 00:19:01,983
- I'll go after you.
- I don't want to run.

311
00:19:01,983 --> 00:19:03,585
- I'll go after you.
- No!

312
00:19:03,585 --> 00:19:06,221
No... No, don't stop.

313
00:19:06,221 --> 00:19:08,089
Come on.

314
00:19:10,592 --> 00:19:12,160
Are you serious?

315
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,729
Do you really have to call
Grandfather Garp about that?

316
00:19:14,729 --> 00:19:17,265
You just made the mess bigger.

317
00:19:17,265 --> 00:19:19,567
Grandfather Garp is the least
of your concerns.

318
00:19:19,567 --> 00:19:21,569
What were you thinking, Florence?

319
00:19:21,569 --> 00:19:23,738
Why did you confront Mr. Villarico?

320
00:19:23,738 --> 00:19:25,440
Because he is hurting Camille.

321
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,108
Do you think I'll just let it go?

322
00:19:27,108 --> 00:19:29,077
What if it's you who got hurt?

323
00:19:29,077 --> 00:19:30,578
Did I get hurt?

324
00:19:30,578 --> 00:19:32,080
No, right?

325
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:34,182
Because we arrived, Florence.

326
00:19:34,182 --> 00:19:37,485
Even if you didn't arrive,
I can protect myself.

327
00:19:37,485 --> 00:19:39,954
So stop being protective, Ferell guys.

328
00:19:39,954 --> 00:19:42,979
I'm not a damsel in distress that needs
a knight in shining armor

329
00:19:42,979 --> 00:19:44,526
who will save me.

330
00:19:44,526 --> 00:19:47,962
You know you can't do it
on your own all the time.

331
00:19:47,962 --> 00:19:51,232
I agree. From now, just stick with us.

332
00:19:51,232 --> 00:19:55,536
A Ferell should always be with you,
so you'll be untouchable.

333
00:19:56,271 --> 00:19:59,541
Huh? What? You'll keep an eye on me?

334
00:19:59,541 --> 00:20:04,412
And then, you'll interfere with my decisions
in life, right?

335
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:07,449
Thanks for your concern, but no thanks.

336
00:20:07,449 --> 00:20:08,719
No!

337
00:20:11,853 --> 00:20:13,388
Ouch!

338
00:20:13,388 --> 00:20:15,924
Florence is so brave, isn't she?

339
00:20:15,924 --> 00:20:18,226
That's what these two guys like...

340
00:20:18,226 --> 00:20:22,630
Strong, independent, and annoying women.

341
00:20:28,388 --> 00:20:31,328
Don Rogelio, he's here already.

342
00:20:31,328 --> 00:20:33,263
Good afternoon, Sir.

343
00:20:35,309 --> 00:20:36,569
Don Rogelio...

344
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:41,201
Again, I'm sorry I wasn't able
to attend our meeting.

345
00:20:41,201 --> 00:20:43,816
Something happened earlier.

346
00:20:43,816 --> 00:20:46,785
Camille had some trouble in school.

347
00:20:46,785 --> 00:20:50,522
And to make matters worse,

348
00:20:50,522 --> 00:20:54,109
I had a confrontation
with Don Ferell's grandsons.

349
00:20:56,462 --> 00:20:58,173
Really?

350
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:01,900
Yes, Sir, and a...

351
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,984
A Ferell woman started it.

352
00:21:05,738 --> 00:21:07,867
A Ferell woman?

353
00:21:14,227 --> 00:21:17,100
Oh, Florence, can we talk?

354
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,067
It's about...

355
00:21:18,067 --> 00:21:21,117
Antonia, I know about your past with Nero.

356
00:21:21,117 --> 00:21:23,022
- But I hope...
- Oh, Florence, stop.

357
00:21:23,022 --> 00:21:26,099
We won't be talking about Nero.

358
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:28,466
Whatever is going on between you and him,

359
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:30,862
it's really none of my concern.

360
00:21:32,187 --> 00:21:34,237
We won't be talking about that?

361
00:21:34,238 --> 00:21:38,804
Yes, but anyway, I just want to remind you

362
00:21:38,804 --> 00:21:41,466
about our meeting later
with the student heads

363
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:42,710
about the ball.

364
00:21:42,710 --> 00:21:45,880
Your department will spearhead it, right?

365
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:48,182
I hope you've already prepared a plan.

366
00:21:48,182 --> 00:21:51,256
Yes, I've collected the suggestions

367
00:21:51,256 --> 00:21:53,787
of my fellow Com Arts department students.

368
00:21:53,787 --> 00:21:56,357
I'll be presenting our plans later.

369
00:21:56,357 --> 00:21:57,424
Perfect.

370
00:21:57,424 --> 00:21:59,893
Well, I'll see you around.

371
00:22:09,236 --> 00:22:11,304
A Ferell woman?

372
00:22:12,106 --> 00:22:15,308
Yes, Sir. There's a Ferell woman in GU.

373
00:22:17,111 --> 00:22:18,912
Are you sure?

374
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:23,817
As far as I know,
Garpidio doesn't have a granddaughter.

375
00:22:24,685 --> 00:22:28,321
Well, those boys claim
that she's a Ferell too.

376
00:22:29,356 --> 00:22:33,561
But, it's the least of my concern.

377
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:37,764
What worries me is that,
Don Ferell might pick on us.

378
00:22:38,566 --> 00:22:42,036
In the middle of our confrontation, Sir...

379
00:22:42,036 --> 00:22:45,806
one of his grandsons called him.

380
00:22:45,806 --> 00:22:47,474
And I'm so worried, Sir,

381
00:22:47,474 --> 00:22:50,678
because the highway project that you gave me

382
00:22:50,678 --> 00:22:54,214
is dealing
with one of the properties of Don Ferell.

383
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:59,153
We need to fix this.

384
00:22:59,153 --> 00:23:02,155
We cannot afford another delay
in this project.

385
00:23:03,891 --> 00:23:05,992
What are we going to do, Sir?

386
00:23:07,161 --> 00:23:09,095
Let me handle this.

387
00:23:20,908 --> 00:23:22,943
Excuse me, Don Ferell.

388
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:27,714
You have a phone call, Sir, from Don Rogelio.

389
00:23:29,683 --> 00:23:31,952
Still alive, Rogelio?

390
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:34,888
I should ask you that question.

391
00:23:34,888 --> 00:23:38,125
Bad weeds take a long time to die.

392
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:44,397
Let's give ourselves another ten years
and see who is the worse weed.

393
00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:47,701
Alright.

394
00:23:47,701 --> 00:23:49,470
So, what's with this call?

395
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:51,739
Is the world ending?

396
00:23:51,739 --> 00:23:54,541
No, not yet.

397
00:23:55,209 --> 00:23:57,945
But one of my men, George,

398
00:23:57,945 --> 00:24:01,848
had an unfortunate encounter
with your grandchildren.

399
00:24:03,484 --> 00:24:06,120
Why don't I pay you a visit,

400
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:09,155
so we can talk about this problem?

401
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:14,695
Welcome, everyone.

402
00:24:14,695 --> 00:24:18,032
I'm excited about the big projects
with all student representatives.

403
00:24:18,032 --> 00:24:20,177
Aira is here on behalf of Aylip,

404
00:24:20,177 --> 00:24:22,919
who has always been supportive
of the grand GU Ball.

405
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:27,547
And because of the hosting disaster
of the Philosophy department,

406
00:24:27,547 --> 00:24:30,878
I'm sure anything that we will do this year
will be a success.

407
00:24:30,878 --> 00:24:33,447
So, let's turn it over to Florence,

408
00:24:33,447 --> 00:24:35,930
the Communication Arts representative.

409
00:24:35,930 --> 00:24:39,386
She and her department
are the hosts this year.

410
00:24:39,386 --> 00:24:41,196
And in the history of the grand ball,

411
00:24:41,196 --> 00:24:44,591
Com Arts has had
the most memorable and powerful impact.

412
00:24:44,591 --> 00:24:46,493
We set the standards.

413
00:24:46,493 --> 00:24:49,596
So, let's hear it from Florence.

414
00:24:49,596 --> 00:24:52,266
Actually, I compiled all the suggestions

415
00:24:52,266 --> 00:24:55,436
of the student leaders of my department,

416
00:24:55,436 --> 00:24:59,973
each one is representing an organization
under Communication Arts.

417
00:24:59,973 --> 00:25:03,344
Yes, and it was fun
because for the first time,

418
00:25:03,344 --> 00:25:06,246
everyone was given a chance
to give suggestions,

419
00:25:06,246 --> 00:25:09,383
and Florence listened to every one of us.

420
00:25:09,383 --> 00:25:10,967
Of course.

421
00:25:10,968 --> 00:25:16,757
First, someone suggested
that we do it like a Coachella music festival.

422
00:25:16,757 --> 00:25:17,968
That's nice.

423
00:25:17,968 --> 00:25:20,171
I've actually been to several Coachellas,

424
00:25:20,171 --> 00:25:22,940
and if we can replicate the atmosphere,

425
00:25:22,940 --> 00:25:24,642
that would really be amazing.

426
00:25:24,642 --> 00:25:27,918
Not to mention,
singing and dancing to our favorite music.

427
00:25:27,918 --> 00:25:30,418
Singing and dancing...

428
00:25:30,418 --> 00:25:33,748
Okay... next suggestion.

429
00:25:33,748 --> 00:25:34,983
Le Bal des Débutantes.

430
00:25:34,983 --> 00:25:36,418
Someone suggested that too.

431
00:25:36,418 --> 00:25:38,119
Oh! I prefer that.

432
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,184
Among the Ferells,

433
00:25:39,184 --> 00:25:42,490
I was the one who attended
an event like that in Paris.

434
00:25:42,490 --> 00:25:44,359
That's really interesting.

435
00:25:44,359 --> 00:25:45,560
It's not that fun,

436
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:50,465
but the event is well-executed
and choreographed.

437
00:25:50,465 --> 00:25:51,733
Next suggestion...

438
00:25:51,733 --> 00:25:56,571
someone suggested that we do it
like Il Ballo del Doge.

439
00:25:56,571 --> 00:25:58,440
A masquerade ball.

440
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:00,342
That one is fun.

441
00:26:00,342 --> 00:26:03,518
Fun because you can hide your ugly face.

442
00:26:06,047 --> 00:26:10,118
Florence, what's your decision?

443
00:26:10,118 --> 00:26:13,788
Actually, the truth is,
all the suggestions are beautiful, right?

444
00:26:13,788 --> 00:26:18,866
But for me, whatever this body wants,

445
00:26:18,866 --> 00:26:20,262
we can go for that direction.

446
00:26:20,262 --> 00:26:26,067
What I want is for our ball to
have a deeper meaning this year.

447
00:26:26,768 --> 00:26:31,539
So, what do you mean by that, Florence?

448
00:26:31,539 --> 00:26:36,044
The ball should be more than
our fancy dresses or big venue,

449
00:26:36,044 --> 00:26:38,413
expensive food.

450
00:26:38,413 --> 00:26:40,882
I want to make it a fundraising event

451
00:26:40,882 --> 00:26:44,418
for the communities who are in need.

452
00:26:45,259 --> 00:26:48,790
We can mount a simple ball,

453
00:26:48,790 --> 00:26:55,354
but if we were to spend
a huge amount of money

454
00:26:55,354 --> 00:26:58,133
because it's GU's grand ball,

455
00:26:58,133 --> 00:27:03,377
I hope we don't take for granted the reality
of living hand-to-mouth,

456
00:27:03,377 --> 00:27:07,909
because not everyone here in GU is well-off.

457
00:27:07,909 --> 00:27:12,180
Some people work every day
so their families can eat.

458
00:27:12,180 --> 00:27:16,818
So, if you're going to ask me,
I want it simple but elegant.

459
00:27:16,818 --> 00:27:20,088
Fun but there's meaning
outside our university,

460
00:27:20,088 --> 00:27:22,690
and we'll be able to help others.

461
00:27:26,961 --> 00:27:28,663
The meeting earlier was okay, right?

462
00:27:28,663 --> 00:27:31,800
- Yes.
- Hey, Florence, you're so good.

463
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:33,168
Good job.

464
00:27:33,168 --> 00:27:34,802
Thank you.

465
00:27:36,971 --> 00:27:38,940
That's weird.

466
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:40,308
Why?

467
00:27:40,308 --> 00:27:43,411
She's an Aylip, and she's being kind to you.

468
00:27:43,411 --> 00:27:46,314
It looks like you're no longer
a persona-non-grata to them.

469
00:27:46,314 --> 00:27:49,117
You're done being a TWPS.
(*The Worst Person in School)

470
00:27:49,117 --> 00:27:50,185
I hope so.

471
00:27:50,185 --> 00:27:52,687
I don't want to be a TWPS anymore.

472
00:27:54,656 --> 00:27:56,257
Florence.

473
00:27:57,058 --> 00:27:58,293
Antonia.

474
00:27:58,293 --> 00:28:00,695
I really like your ideas.

475
00:28:00,695 --> 00:28:03,504
I just feel bad, because you're right.

476
00:28:03,504 --> 00:28:05,162
We, who are born into privilege,

477
00:28:05,162 --> 00:28:09,303
we tend to take for granted
the reality that exists outside of us.

478
00:28:12,073 --> 00:28:14,109
It's not yet too late.

479
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:15,443
More or less,

480
00:28:15,443 --> 00:28:20,700
the capitalists have ten years
to save the planet, our world,

481
00:28:20,701 --> 00:28:24,638
or else, well then, we'll all die.

482
00:28:26,441 --> 00:28:28,916
I equally love your sense of humor.

483
00:28:28,916 --> 00:28:31,512
We should discuss the details next meeting.

484
00:28:31,512 --> 00:28:34,215
I have some ideas
that we can use for the ball.

485
00:28:34,215 --> 00:28:35,683
It was really nice talking to you.

486
00:28:35,683 --> 00:28:37,351
I'll see you later.

487
00:28:40,955 --> 00:28:43,564
Does she think you're joking?

488
00:28:43,564 --> 00:28:45,903
Isn't she aware with the recent IPCC Report?

489
00:28:45,903 --> 00:28:49,563
If we won't be doing anything,
earth will vanish.

490
00:28:51,300 --> 00:28:52,901
Why?

491
00:28:54,470 --> 00:28:57,139
I just feel guilty.

492
00:28:57,139 --> 00:28:58,207
With what?

493
00:28:58,207 --> 00:29:00,542
About you and Nero?

494
00:29:01,494 --> 00:29:04,480
Florence, it's over between her and Nero,

495
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,415
and you're together now.

496
00:29:06,415 --> 00:29:08,917
And it looks like she has moved on already.

497
00:29:10,786 --> 00:29:14,303
Oh well, I'll just tell you
the whole story next time.

498
00:29:14,303 --> 00:29:16,191
What? Which one?

499
00:29:17,259 --> 00:29:20,829
Well, next time... next time.

500
00:29:23,566 --> 00:29:25,267
Let's see each other later.

501
00:29:25,267 --> 00:29:26,902
There's someone I want to talk to.

502
00:29:26,902 --> 00:29:28,470
Bye.

503
00:29:29,672 --> 00:29:31,373
Aira!

504
00:29:31,373 --> 00:29:33,008
Aira...

505
00:29:36,478 --> 00:29:38,547
Can we talk?

506
00:29:44,796 --> 00:29:47,122
What do you need?

507
00:29:47,122 --> 00:29:49,358
Are you here to gloat?

508
00:29:49,358 --> 00:29:52,106
To celebrate
that Camille and I are miserable.

509
00:29:54,465 --> 00:29:56,012
No.

510
00:29:56,832 --> 00:29:59,777
Actually, I want to talk to you.

511
00:29:59,777 --> 00:30:03,683
I want to check on you and Camille.

512
00:30:05,341 --> 00:30:07,384
You guys can go ahead.

513
00:30:14,767 --> 00:30:17,544
Honestly, she's having a hard time.

514
00:30:19,291 --> 00:30:20,133
She got suspended,

515
00:30:20,133 --> 00:30:23,105
that's why the last time I heard,
her father is fuming mad.

516
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:28,269
If you only know her father, Florence.

517
00:30:28,269 --> 00:30:31,013
You won't believe what he is capable of.

518
00:30:31,013 --> 00:30:34,549
No, I believe you, Aira.

519
00:30:34,549 --> 00:30:36,667
Yesterday, while I'm on my way to school,

520
00:30:36,667 --> 00:30:40,055
I saw Camille's father hurting her.

521
00:30:43,477 --> 00:30:44,995
That's expected.

522
00:30:47,901 --> 00:30:52,126
I've known for years
that Camille's dad is abusive.

523
00:30:53,541 --> 00:30:55,968
He wants Camille to be always on top

524
00:30:55,968 --> 00:30:58,923
that's why with just a little mistake,
my friend would be slapped.

525
00:31:01,473 --> 00:31:03,980
I remember the first time I met her.

526
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:07,439
Eleventh place?

527
00:31:11,686 --> 00:31:13,900
When we received the letter,

528
00:31:13,901 --> 00:31:15,033
I was expecting

529
00:31:15,033 --> 00:31:19,356
that at least you'd get in the top five
of those who took the exam.

530
00:31:20,933 --> 00:31:22,403
Eleventh?

531
00:31:22,403 --> 00:31:23,498
How come?

532
00:31:23,498 --> 00:31:26,174
You didn't even make it to the top ten.

533
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:29,015
Dad?

534
00:31:29,015 --> 00:31:30,784
Dad...

535
00:31:31,506 --> 00:31:33,873
I'm so sorry.

536
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:38,846
You're nothing but a big disappointment.

537
00:31:38,846 --> 00:31:43,017
I'm so sorry, Dad.

538
00:31:48,189 --> 00:31:50,633
That was the first time I saw her.

539
00:31:53,061 --> 00:31:54,781
I'm sorry.

540
00:31:57,285 --> 00:31:59,304
Why are you apologizing?

541
00:32:01,492 --> 00:32:03,779
We've been horrible to you.

542
00:32:03,779 --> 00:32:07,074
We did a lot of things
so you'll be miserable.

543
00:32:08,645 --> 00:32:13,907
Even then,
no one deserves to get hurt that way.

544
00:32:15,919 --> 00:32:18,113
I don't want to make excuses.

545
00:32:19,022 --> 00:32:21,998
Because what we did to you was really wrong.

546
00:32:23,793 --> 00:32:28,972
But maybe, I was enabling Camille...

547
00:32:30,466 --> 00:32:33,566
because I know the miserable life
that she has.

548
00:32:38,408 --> 00:32:41,083
I'm so sorry for that, Florence.

549
00:32:42,979 --> 00:32:45,648
If only we got to know you better,

550
00:32:45,648 --> 00:32:47,953
Camille and I will like you as well.

551
00:32:49,752 --> 00:32:53,144
But no, we judged you.

552
00:32:54,163 --> 00:32:57,977
And worst, we made you feel
that you don't belong in this world.

553
00:33:01,164 --> 00:33:03,132
That's okay.

554
00:33:03,132 --> 00:33:07,207
It's never too late to heal and forgive.

555
00:33:07,207 --> 00:33:09,195
That's why I want to talk to you,

556
00:33:09,195 --> 00:33:12,281
and I want to talk to Camille as well.

557
00:33:15,445 --> 00:33:17,501
Are you sure?

558
00:33:26,900 --> 00:33:28,189
Why are we here?

559
00:33:28,189 --> 00:33:30,834
Why are you making me hurry?

560
00:33:35,565 --> 00:33:37,467
What is this, Aira?

561
00:33:37,467 --> 00:33:39,469
Is this a trap?

562
00:33:39,469 --> 00:33:43,139
Did you make me come here
so she can laugh at me?

563
00:33:43,139 --> 00:33:45,355
So they can gang up on me?

564
00:33:46,143 --> 00:33:47,748
Camille, no.

565
00:33:49,780 --> 00:33:52,589
Then, what is this for?

566
00:33:52,589 --> 00:33:55,425
Is she doing a blog for bullies?

567
00:33:56,753 --> 00:33:58,487
No, Camille.

568
00:33:59,879 --> 00:34:05,395
This is us showing you that we understand
what you're going through now.

569
00:34:05,395 --> 00:34:09,508
We want to assure you
that whatever you're going through,

570
00:34:09,508 --> 00:34:11,534
we are here for you.

571
00:34:11,534 --> 00:34:13,569
And if you need help,

572
00:34:13,569 --> 00:34:16,722
we're ready to help you, whatever that is.

573
00:34:17,774 --> 00:34:20,342
Why are you doing this to me?

574
00:34:22,078 --> 00:34:28,168
Why are you so kind to me
after all that I did to you?

575
00:34:30,402 --> 00:34:36,165
Because, Camille, I believe
that everyone deserves a second chance.

576
00:34:36,165 --> 00:34:38,745
Except for Hitler.

577
00:34:38,745 --> 00:34:42,766
But you, you deserve that.

578
00:34:43,979 --> 00:34:47,107
Why are you so kind?

579
00:34:47,107 --> 00:34:50,228
You're annoying.

580
00:34:57,714 --> 00:34:59,682
I'm sorry.

581
00:34:59,682 --> 00:35:01,084
That's okay.

582
00:35:01,084 --> 00:35:02,719
I'm sorry for being mean.

583
00:35:02,719 --> 00:35:06,619
I'm sorry for everything.

584
00:35:06,619 --> 00:35:08,203
That's okay, Camille.

585
00:35:08,203 --> 00:35:09,325
Stop crying...

586
00:35:09,325 --> 00:35:11,160
Don't cry anymore.

587
00:35:11,995 --> 00:35:16,332
Don't cry, don't cry.

588
00:35:16,332 --> 00:35:18,118
Just smile.

589
00:35:19,439 --> 00:35:21,637
Cheers!

590
00:35:21,637 --> 00:35:24,207
Wow, that's great.

591
00:35:24,207 --> 00:35:25,908
I told you, Florence.

592
00:35:25,908 --> 00:35:27,310
Start talking about the grand ball,

593
00:35:27,310 --> 00:35:29,979
and the process of healing will be faster.

594
00:35:29,979 --> 00:35:34,350
You're really good in exposing people.

595
00:35:34,350 --> 00:35:38,200
Don't worry. You're still my bestie.

596
00:35:38,200 --> 00:35:41,337
I like you both,
and I would love to be friends with you.

597
00:35:41,337 --> 00:35:43,567
But in the hierarchy of friends,

598
00:35:43,567 --> 00:35:45,908
Camille is still on top of my list.

599
00:35:45,908 --> 00:35:48,410
Stop it.

600
00:35:48,410 --> 00:35:51,733
That's where you start looking down
on others,

601
00:35:51,734 --> 00:35:54,916
with that hierarchy.

602
00:35:56,018 --> 00:35:58,267
- Wow, changed person.
- Yeah.

603
00:35:58,267 --> 00:36:02,624
If I find out that you two are starting
to be mean and be bullies,

604
00:36:02,624 --> 00:36:04,360
you'll answer to me.

605
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:07,896
- That's right.
- That's right!

606
00:36:07,896 --> 00:36:10,066
True...

607
00:36:14,269 --> 00:36:15,904
Okay.

608
00:36:15,904 --> 00:36:19,174
I think that is your superpower, Florence.

609
00:36:19,174 --> 00:36:23,178
Everybody eventually wants
to be friends with you.

610
00:36:23,178 --> 00:36:27,949
Even Antonia, who is the former ex
of your boyfriend Nero.

611
00:36:28,717 --> 00:36:30,136
Why?

612
00:36:33,517 --> 00:36:36,592
I want to change my life.

613
00:36:37,326 --> 00:36:44,200
I don't want to say bad things
about others, but...

614
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:46,649
Florence deserves to know.

615
00:36:48,003 --> 00:36:49,505
Yeah.

616
00:36:49,505 --> 00:36:53,042
It's not that I want to badmouth others,

617
00:36:53,042 --> 00:36:57,482
but... be careful of Antonia.

618
00:36:58,088 --> 00:37:00,164
Why?

619
00:37:00,164 --> 00:37:03,252
Well, she's the real deal, Florence.

620
00:37:03,252 --> 00:37:06,822
I mean, I admit that I'm not a good girl,

621
00:37:06,822 --> 00:37:09,235
I'm an in-and-out mean girl,

622
00:37:09,235 --> 00:37:15,909
but Antonia seems like
she's hiding a different persona...

623
00:37:15,909 --> 00:37:18,930
and that's scarier.

624
00:37:18,930 --> 00:37:20,936
She's the Queen Bee.

625
00:37:20,936 --> 00:37:23,439
And do you think the queen will easily agree

626
00:37:23,439 --> 00:37:25,666
that you'll get one of her belongings?

627
00:37:33,782 --> 00:37:35,437
Those two were something else.

628
00:37:35,437 --> 00:37:38,253
That's because they're used to talking about
a lot of nonsense.

629
00:37:38,253 --> 00:37:42,749
But I don't think so, Antonia looks nice.

630
00:37:44,164 --> 00:37:47,625
But Antonia seems like
she's hiding a different persona...

631
00:37:47,625 --> 00:37:50,659
and that's scarier.

632
00:37:50,659 --> 00:37:52,768
She's the Queen Bee.

633
00:37:52,768 --> 00:37:55,237
And do you think the queen will easily agree

634
00:37:55,237 --> 00:37:58,006
that you'll get one of her belongings?

635
00:37:58,006 --> 00:37:59,575
Florence?

636
00:37:59,575 --> 00:38:00,576
Florence?

637
00:38:00,576 --> 00:38:01,778
Yes?

638
00:38:02,778 --> 00:38:03,984
Is there a problem?

639
00:38:03,984 --> 00:38:07,422
Hurry up, Don Ferell is asking for you.

640
00:38:08,350 --> 00:38:10,053
Why?

641
00:38:10,053 --> 00:38:11,453
Do I look like a gossip-monger to you?

642
00:38:11,453 --> 00:38:13,555
Why? What did you do this time?

643
00:38:13,555 --> 00:38:17,125
Come on. You hurry up.
Leave that... Leave that!

644
00:38:23,959 --> 00:38:25,892
Excuse me, Don Ferell.

645
00:38:25,892 --> 00:38:29,037
Florence is here already.

646
00:38:29,037 --> 00:38:30,531
Grandfather Garp?

647
00:38:31,872 --> 00:38:34,899
So you're Florence Dela Cruz?

648
00:38:52,979 --> 00:38:56,266
Florence, I'd like you
to meet George Villarico.

649
00:38:56,267 --> 00:39:01,351
He's an associate of Don Rogelio Almero.

650
00:39:01,351 --> 00:39:05,283
- And this dashing gentleman here is...
- I am Rogelio Almero.

651
00:39:08,812 --> 00:39:13,231
This guy, George,
claims that you attacked him.

652
00:39:14,032 --> 00:39:15,647
Is it true?

653
00:39:21,246 --> 00:39:24,393
Yes, Grandfather Garp, that's true.

654
00:39:24,393 --> 00:39:25,594
So it's true.

655
00:39:25,594 --> 00:39:28,891
I kicked him on his...

656
00:39:28,891 --> 00:39:31,294
Beep... Beep, beep...

657
00:39:33,117 --> 00:39:35,671
First, why did you meddle?

658
00:39:35,671 --> 00:39:38,693
He was just talking to his daughter.

659
00:39:38,693 --> 00:39:41,051
And then when he asked you
to leave him alone,

660
00:39:41,051 --> 00:39:43,330
you kicked him there.

661
00:39:43,968 --> 00:39:46,281
That's very disrespectful, Florence.

662
00:39:46,281 --> 00:39:48,916
I cannot tolerate such behavior.

663
00:39:48,916 --> 00:39:50,700
Cannot be.

664
00:39:55,561 --> 00:40:01,351
I'm sorry if I kicked you on the... beep.

665
00:40:02,771 --> 00:40:04,870
But, Grandfather Garp,

666
00:40:04,870 --> 00:40:08,974
if I need to do it again, I'll do it.

667
00:40:08,974 --> 00:40:11,510
What? You'll do it again?

668
00:40:11,510 --> 00:40:12,711
Why?

669
00:40:12,711 --> 00:40:16,148
Because he was physically hurting his daughter.

670
00:40:16,148 --> 00:40:17,817
What reached you was a fake story

671
00:40:17,817 --> 00:40:20,786
that I just hurt him without a valid reason.

672
00:40:20,786 --> 00:40:22,868
I was defending Camille.

673
00:40:22,868 --> 00:40:26,292
And that's what my mother and father taught me,
Grandfather Garp.

674
00:40:26,292 --> 00:40:29,662
If I see someone getting abused,
I need to help.

675
00:40:29,662 --> 00:40:31,763
George, is this true?

676
00:40:32,832 --> 00:40:36,153
Pardon me for what I did, Sir,
please let me explain.

677
00:40:36,153 --> 00:40:37,722
I'm under a lot of pressure

678
00:40:37,722 --> 00:40:40,966
and when I found out
that Camille has a problem in school,

679
00:40:40,966 --> 00:40:43,401
I completely lost my temper.

680
00:40:43,401 --> 00:40:45,238
Let's talk later.

681
00:40:49,556 --> 00:40:52,341
What you did is admirable, Miss.

682
00:40:53,334 --> 00:40:57,204
I commend your courage
in standing up for others.

683
00:41:00,422 --> 00:41:01,300
I felt it right away

684
00:41:01,300 --> 00:41:04,256
that she was Celestina,
my missing granddaughter...

685
00:41:04,256 --> 00:41:08,932
Son, I think I found your daughter.

686
00:41:08,932 --> 00:41:11,335
I have found Celestina.

687
00:41:11,335 --> 00:41:13,203
What?

688
00:41:13,203 --> 00:41:16,042
The on-and-off battle
between me and Don Rogelio

689
00:41:16,042 --> 00:41:18,691
goes a long way back.

690
00:41:18,691 --> 00:41:21,719
And it's not just about politics.

691
00:41:21,719 --> 00:41:25,673
Don't tell me, Grandfather,
you also had a competition on love?

692
00:41:25,673 --> 00:41:28,067
Yup.

693
00:41:28,067 --> 00:41:29,646
Florence?

694
00:41:31,345 --> 00:41:35,315
Look, I'm sorry
that we met under unfortunate circumstances.

695
00:41:35,315 --> 00:41:37,125
I understand.

696
00:41:37,125 --> 00:41:38,627
There's nothing to worry about.

697
00:41:38,627 --> 00:41:41,195
Oh, but look, what do we have here?

698
00:41:41,195 --> 00:41:42,930
Is Mr. Henry your favorite too?

699
00:41:42,930 --> 00:41:44,164
Mr. Henry's chicken?

700
00:41:44,164 --> 00:41:45,499
You, too?

701
00:41:45,499 --> 00:41:46,781
Is that your favorite?

702
00:41:46,781 --> 00:41:49,574
Actually, I didn't discover this place.

703
00:41:49,574 --> 00:41:52,640
It was my daughter-in-law, Alyanna.

704
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:56,076
It was suggested to me by my friend
who owns an IT company.

705
00:41:56,076 --> 00:41:59,522
He sent me a computer graphics expert.

706
00:41:59,522 --> 00:42:00,953
Look.

707
00:42:00,953 --> 00:42:03,168
That is the rendered picture.

708
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:06,221
That is Celestina's picture.

709
00:42:09,493 --> 00:42:13,915
I have a strong hunch
that this is your missing daughter.

710
00:42:13,915 --> 00:42:15,687
That's Celestina.
